      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1720,
        "height": 250,
        "content": "## One email attachment per child execution\nGmail parent runs serially with one item per call. Same storage, processing, review and notification APIs as upload v4. Unsupported/no attachments get a persisted skipped outcome. Invalid PDF content is rejected by the backend and counted. Uncached calls wait 65 seconds; the backend rate gate remains authoritative. Cache condition reflects the current Gemini configuration; update it when switching model. SMTP is local Mailpit only. No mailbox mutation or deletion. Based on the preserved original template and v4; not a claim of Gmail runtime verification."
      }
    },
